From e49884b11642cd48d204ee75d80e8c92432dd89d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Viljo Marrandi <30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 13:56:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] feat(sim): step the simulation to the next or the
 previous operation

The transport bar has "Previous operation" and "Next operation" buttons,
with Page Up and Page Down. A step moves the playhead to the start of an
operation and pauses there. The readout names the operation. Previous
goes to the start of the current operation, then to the one before it.
The buttons are disabled at the first and the last operation, and while
the stock removal is calculated.

The lookup is on sim::Script (op_starts, next_op_start, prev_op_start,
op_starting_at) in camcraft-sim, so the stand-alone simulator can use it.
An operation with no moves is not on the timeline, so it is no stop. The
stock follows the playhead as for a scrub, and a test compares the
stepped stock with move-by-move playback across a tool change.

Fixes #2608

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
