From c3efcfe7cbb0fec19cfb8849aeadde05fa954f99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Viljo Marrandi <30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 20:11:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] perf(sim): walk the operation starts one time for each
 timeline

Review of PR #2763. The step buttons called the Script lookups in each
frame, and each call walked every segment of the timeline. OpStarts::of
now walks the segments one time; next, prev and op_at are binary
searches over one entry for each operation. The transport keeps the
starts in State beside the cached script, keyed on the script's Arc
(sim_steps::cached_op_starts).

A new test pins the value of each start from the segments, and a UI
test pins that a still frame walks no segment. The Gate map line of
sim_op_step_stock names camcraft_sim::sim.

Refs #2608

